llars ended  up doing a pretty good job of pretty  much making the perfect fish whatever  fish it really is I'm no biologist to  make that damn thing unvisible and make  this at least a little bit more  realistic so there was a bit of  struggling with different things there I  also have to say that a lot of time was  in the end spent on fine-tuning these  and this arch since I've really got the  base down quite quickly  and had a certain idea of what I wanted  to do but when it comes to the really  minor details it really took a lot of  messing about with things to actually  get to a point where I was happy with  how it looks like at this point in time  I wasn't really too happy with the top  of the building since it seemed a bit  too narrow I do like it somewhat but  it's not Roman and it's not even a shape  that I very commonly see so I wanted to  make that a bit higher as well and when  it comes to certain other things and  real life these things I just dressed up  with lots of sculptures along the side  lots of murals and also some letters and  numbers probably alongside the top as  well to whomever they were erected for  or whoever was narcissistic enough to  want to have an arch somewhere on the  plaza somewhere and obviously I can't  really get those things in so there was  just a lot of just opening random  scenery items in the game and seeing  when I could actually do with them the  general idea behind this arch was really  though to tie the Roman area a bit more  together as well like like I said before  having that little sloped area with the  rocks where I basically couldn't do  anything because there's a slope pot and  you can't really attach buildings around  it very easily and it's very awkward  since you can't make a cross see here  either  and like on the other side I got rid of  that problem by basically having the  zero-g roll go over the path having that  small aqueducts and just having a  passage through buildings but it wasn't  quite so easy to make that here so I  want to tell me to at least be able to  expand the Roman area into this  direction but not make it feel like  there are two separate parts like you  have the part which is high up and you  have the part which is lower over here  and that there is no connection really  between them and I guess this was really  my only idea I had to make that happen  like an arch which from here really  makes like all the different paths  actually go toward this arch which is  quite funny considering these saying I  don't know if this is actually in an  English saying as well but considering  me saying that all roads lead to Rome  somewhere but yeah the that's basically  why I felt like I wanted to have this  thing basically as an object which you  could see from the entire area and be  more or less the center point of it  there is probably a better word to  describe it but uh probably said that  enough at this point in time but yeah  that's basically the general idea behind  it and then alongside this thing there  are still a couple of ideas which I have  and a couple of new years which I also  got from Commons which I'm still  thinking about the first thing which  I'll add around here is a restaurants  and I'll probably also have the which  like flat ride the one round flat right  which I haven't placed in the park yet  which I really felt fits quite well with  the Roman theme somehow I have no idea  why I feel that but besides I still need  a flat rights in here somewhere but also  an idea which I got so many requests to  make a Colosseum or which is something  that I might feature in some way but I'm  definitely not going to make a Colosseum  not even a small and I just feel like oh  come on that has done like two amazing  of a job at it already to even try doing  it and I don't really see much of a  point even but what I do love to make  perhaps is an amphitheater or  it's a pronounced right anyway yeah like  one of these little theaters much like  the I think it's Marco Polo theater in  Busch Gardens Williamsburg  because you see theaters a lot in theme  parks obviously and I don't even have  one over here at the moment and what  better theme to do it with then and  roman-themed really I feel so even if I  won't make it a Coliseum which is very  likely I do still want to make a simple  theater alongside the side of this Plaza  somewhere and so basically it will be  filled up with rides and places to go  alongside all of the size of this Plaza  I don't just make it a simple Plaza in  the middle of nowhere which would make  the the arch in the middle quite an  underwhelming thing really so this will  be quite a centerpiece for in this area  but then again I won't really expand the  Roman area much beside that I've been  thinking about the dark ride but I'm not  really sure if that's really manageable  in the time and if it's really worth it  to get the effort to actually build a  full dark ride which I if I do so I  would want to put a lot of efforts into  and I do want to finish this park before  the end of this alpha and also before it  completely crashes and before it reaches  terrible FPS or at least an unworkable  frame it so I probably won't be running  a dark ride so that will really be my  only plans for the Roman area it's  perhaps almost going to double in size  from what it is now or just a bit more  but it's not going to be that huge so  there will still be space left for  different themes and then I'll just have  to at some point decide what the best  themes are I haven't really tried to  much I've tried a couple of Dutch  buildings and as much as I would love to  do the theme I am a little less  confident that I connect [ __ ] and then I  Mia that I can actually do it then the  last time that I announced it since I  tried it and it didn't even work out  that well it's possible but only if you  stretch the theme very much and if you  try to keep it just to the basics it  just turns out very boring so I might do  it but just go not that realistic with  it and have more fantasy details to it  anyway but there are also some other  themes a Viking theme is a possibility  I've also been thinking about an Arabian  theme as similar to an Italian theme as  it is really and those are just the  things that are on my mind at the moment  anyway that's it for this episode  I'm not going to overview this thing  quite yet and I'll really save that  until this general Plaza is finished but  thank you guys for watching this episode  and see you later
 

